   "start_page": 240,
   "summary": "This concluding section of the Ibaraki Prefecture educational roster documents town and village elementary schools (numbers 157 through 492) and kindergartens, followed by private colleges, vocational schools, middle schools, girls' high schools, youth schools, and miscellaneous schools. It also lists specialized institutions under the Home Ministry, Ministry of Transportation, and Ministry of Welfare, including police, railway, and juvenile correction facilities. Each entry details the school's location, founding date, male and female student enrollments, and teaching staff for April and November 1946. The report concludes with an aggregate statistical summary and a reference map of the Kanto region showing prefectures, capitals, and major educational centers.",
